{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1559544428,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDIzMDU1MDU2MA=="},"target":"33705baf68d9344ad26cb76829b1fa2c7c1fb92319c616d5554897b5692c19ed","message":"We decided that in the cmdline, relative is always relative to PWD. This is not what happens in `install`\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad install -d bids -s raw bids/sourcedata\n[INFO   ] Cloning raw into '/tmp/bids/bids/bids/sourcedata' \ninstall(ok): bids/bids/sourcedata (dataset)                                                  \naction summary:\n  add (ok: 2)\n  install (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad subdatasets -d bids\nsubdataset(ok): bids/bids/sourcedata (dataset)\n```\n\nSo while the relative path given as source (`-s`) is treated as being relative to PWD, the target path is treated as being relative to the specified dataset path.\n\nEven like this it doesn't work (pointless and uncalled for `bids/` subdirectory):\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad install -d bids -s raw sourcedata\n[INFO   ] Cloning raw into '/tmp/bids/bids/sourcedata' \ninstall(ok): bids/sourcedata (dataset)                                                       \naction summary:\n  add (ok: 2)\n  install (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad -f json_pp subdatasets -d bids\n{\n  \"gitmodule_name\": \"bids/sourcedata\",\n  \"gitmodule_url\": \"/tmp/raw\",\n  \"parentds\": \"/tmp/bids\",\n  \"path\": \"/tmp/bids/bids/sourcedata\",\n  \"refds\": \"/tmp/bids\",\n  \"type\": \"dataset\"\n}\n```","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1559544543,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDIzMDU1MTIxMA=="},"target":"33705baf68d9344ad26cb76829b1fa2c7c1fb92319c616d5554897b5692c19ed","message":"We decided that in the cmdline, relative is always relative to PWD. This is not what happens in `install`\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad install -d bids -s raw bids/sourcedata\n[INFO   ] Cloning raw into '/tmp/bids/bids/bids/sourcedata' \ninstall(ok): bids/bids/sourcedata (dataset)                                                  \naction summary:\n  add (ok: 2)\n  install (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad subdatasets -d bids\nsubdataset(ok): bids/bids/sourcedata (dataset)\n```\n\nSo while the relative path given as source (`-s`) is treated as being relative to PWD, the target path is treated as being relative to the specified dataset path.\n\nEven like this it doesn't work (pointless and uncalled for `bids/` subdirectory):\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad install -d bids -s raw sourcedata\n[INFO   ] Cloning raw into '/tmp/bids/bids/sourcedata' \ninstall(ok): bids/sourcedata (dataset)                                                       \naction summary:\n  add (ok: 2)\n  install (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad -f json_pp subdatasets -d bids\n{\n  \"gitmodule_name\": \"bids/sourcedata\",\n  \"gitmodule_url\": \"/tmp/raw\",\n  \"parentds\": \"/tmp/bids\",\n  \"path\": \"/tmp/bids/bids/sourcedata\",\n  \"refds\": \"/tmp/bids\",\n  \"type\": \"dataset\"\n}\n```\n\nOnly this gives the desired result:\n\n```\n% datalad -C bids install -d . -s ../raw sourcedata\n[INFO   ] Cloning ../raw into '/tmp/bids/sourcedata' \ninstall(ok): sourcedata (dataset)                                                            \naction summary:\n  add (ok: 2)\n  install (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad -f json_pp subdatasets -d bids\n{\n  \"gitmodule_name\": \"sourcedata\",\n  \"gitmodule_url\": \"/tmp/bids/../raw\",\n  \"parentds\": \"/tmp/bids\",\n  \"path\": \"/tmp/bids/sourcedata\",\n  \"refds\": \"/tmp/bids\",\n  \"type\": \"dataset\"\n}\n```","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1559544